<!DOCTYPE article PUBLIC "-//NLM//DTD Journal Archiving and Interchange DTD v2.3 20070202//EN" "archivearticle.dtd"><article article-type="letter"><?properties open_access?><!-- Original-type: sc--><front><journal-meta><journal-id journal-id-type="nlm-ta">Br J Cancer</journal-id><journal-title>British Journal of Cancer</journal-title><issn pub-type="ppub">0007-0920</issn><issn pub-type="epub">1532-1827</issn><publisher><publisher-name>Nature Publishing Group</publisher-name></publisher></journal-meta><article-meta><article-id pub-id-type="pmid">10408708</article-id><article-id pub-id-type="pmc">2362181</article-id><article-id pub-id-type="pii">6690026</article-id><article-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1038/sj.bjc.6690026</article-id><article-categories><subj-group subj-group-type="heading"><subject>Short Communication</subject></subj-group></article-categories><title-group><article-title>Comparison of the distribution of non-AIDS Kaposi's sarcoma and non-Hodgkin's lymphoma in Europe</article-title></title-group><contrib-group><contrib contrib-type="author"><name><surname>Maso</surname><given-names>L Dal</given-names></name><xref ref-type="aff" rid="aff1">1</xref></contrib><contrib contrib-type="author"><name><surname>Franceschi</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><xref ref-type="aff" rid="aff1">1</xref></contrib><contrib contrib-type="author"><name><surname>Re</surname><given-names>A Lo</given-names></name><xref ref-type="aff" rid="aff1">1</xref></contrib><contrib contrib-type="author"><name><surname>Vecchia</surname><given-names>C La</given-names></name><xref ref-type="aff" rid="aff2">2</xref><xref ref-type="aff" rid="aff3">3</xref></contrib></contrib-group><aff id="aff1"><label>1</label>Servizio di Epidemiologia, Centro di Riferimento Oncologico, Via Pedemontana Occ.le, Aviano, 12 33081 (PN), Italy</aff><aff id="aff2"><label>2</label>Istituto di Ricerche Farmacologiche &#x02018;M Negri&#x02019;, via Eritrea 62, Milano 20157, Italy</aff><aff id="aff3"><label>3</label>Istituto di Statistica Medica e Biometria,Un&#x000ed;versit&#x000e0; degli Studi, Milano, Italy</aff><author-notes><corresp id="caf1"><label>*</label>Author for correspondence: </corresp></author-notes><pub-date pub-type="epub"><day>24</day><month>09</month><year>1999</year></pub-date><pub-date pub-type="ppub"><month>01</month><year>1999</year></pub-date><volume>79</volume><issue>1</issue><fpage>161</fpage><lpage>163</lpage><history><date date-type="received"><day>18</day><month>03</month><year>1998</year></date><date date-type="rev-recd"><day>12</day><month>05</month><year>1998</year></date><date date-type="accepted"><day>26</day><month>05</month><year>1988</year></date></history><copyright-statement>Copyright 1999, Cancer Research Campaign</copyright-statement><copyright-year>1999</copyright-year><permissions><copyright-holder>Cancer Research Campaign</copyright-holder></permissions><abstract><p>To evaluate whether some form of mild immunosuppression may influence the geographical distribution of non-AIDS Kaposi's sarcoma (KS), we correlated incidence rates of KS and non-Hodgkin's lymphoma in individuals aged 60 or more in 18 European countries and Israel. Significant positive correlations emerged but, within highest risk countries (i.e.Italy and Israel), internal correlations were inconsistent. &#x000a9; 1999 Cancer Research Campaign</p></abstract><kwd-group><kwd>Kaposi's sarcoma</kwd><kwd>non-Hodgkin's lymphoma</kwd><kwd>incidence</kwd><kwd>Europe</kwd><kwd>immunodeficiency</kwd></kwd-group></article-meta></front></article>